BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Module: CO Careers Talk\; CO Year 1 COMP General\; CO Year 1 JM
 C General\nEvent category: M - Careers Event\nGroup: CO Computing Year 1 (
 BEng/MEng)\; CO Joint Maths & Computing Year 1 (BEng/MEng)\nRoom: HXLY 308
 \nStaff: Carruthers\, Richard J\; Dallison\, Katie J\; Valera-Espina\, Mar
 ia\nEvent id: 5028609\nNotes: Working with others is a core part of a DoC 
 degree\, but group work can sometimes be challenging. This session explore
 s how different personalities and working styles can strengthen team proje
 cts and why learning to work effectively with others is a key professional
  skill.\n\nIn the age of AI and rapidly evolving technology\, employers in
 creasingly look for interns and graduates who combine strong technical abi
 lity with human skills. Skills such as communication\, collaboration\, lea
 dership\, and conflict resolution are essential for turning technical know
 ledge into real impact.\n\nThis interactive session will help you reflect 
 on and develop the teamwork skills needed to succeed at Imperial and in in
 dustry. Whether you’re working on group coursework\, hackathons\, or fut
 ure workplace projects\, strong collaboration can make the difference betw
 een an average outcome and an outstanding one. In this session you will le
 arn how to:\n• Work more effectively in group projects\n• Communicate 
 ideas clearly with teammates\n• Manage differing viewpoints and resolve 
 conflicts\n• Contribute to stronger team outcomes and better grades\n\nS
 trong teamwork not only improves your university experience\, it’s also 
 one of the most valuable skills you can demonstrate to future employers.
UID:040000008200E00074C5B7101A82E008000000009F55190F3D30DC01000000000000000
 010000000842D1E245940B046BBFF101622483E04
SUMMARY:CO Professional Skills Training (Improving teamwork for better grad
 es)
